ad_before": 12.01, "lead_after": 11.99, "points_lost": -0.02, "best": "H4"}, {"turn": 63, "color": "B", "move": "pass", "lead_before": 11.99, "lead_after": 12.0, "points_lost": -0.01, "best": "F9"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "A 21-point lead handed back", "summary": "Black, the 12k, won by 12 after the game swung twice. White was 21.4 points ahead after the 12k's H7 on turn 15. Opus 5.5 then lost 8.5, 12.3 and 9.2 points on turns 16, 18 and 20, which put Black ahead by 5.1. The lead stayed between 12 and 14 points for the rest of the game, and both sides passed at the end.", "moments": [{"turn": 15, "text": "The 12k played H7, extending the row-7 wall along White's row-6 line. It lost 15.6 points and took Black's lead from -5.8 to -21.4, the biggest swing of the game and the 12k's only blunder. The engine preferred D2."}, {"turn": 16, "text": "With the lead in hand, Opus 5.5 played G4 and lost 8.5 points. Black's lead moved from -21.4 only to -12.9, so White was still well ahead, but the engine's H3 would have kept more of it."}, {"turn": 18, "text": "E4 was Opus 5.5's worst move, losing 12.3 points. The position was -13.1 for Black before it and -0.8 after, so almost the whole advantage went in one move. The engine wanted C2."}, {"turn": 20, "text": "D4 lost another 9.2 points and turned a -4.1 position into +5.1 for Black. Black's D3, E3 and F3 now formed a row under White's stones, and from here on Black was ahead. The engine again preferred C2."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "J3 lost 6.1 points and moved the lead from +2.4 to +8.5 for Black. It was Opus 5.5's fourth and last blunder. C4 two moves later lost 4.1 more and put Black at +12.8, near the final margin."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "after.py places one player-named move on a pasted board, removes captured stones and prints each group's liberties, while count.py and libs.py only count territory and liberties on the given position. None of them generates or ranks candidates or looks ahead, so the player chose the moves itself.", "stop": false}}